From f6b102334b0c26e149ea1c4b6e468f83fad4f192 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 14:35:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(tui_gateway): preserve undelivered replay on non-Stop
 interrupts [daveey]

Send-now, rewind, deletion and plugin interrupt origins stop the current turn,
not automation notices that have never reached its transcript. Scope the replay
cancellation fence to plain Stop origins in both interrupt RPC paths while
preserving the existing interruption/queue policy.

Exercise the durable successful-context fence through the actual prompt worker,
with unpersisted, later-joined and foreign-profile controls. Exercise admitted
crash recovery through the actual consumer, not a direct journal settle call.

Proof: non-Stop regression reproduced eight failures on reviewed head; both
compute and in-process paths pass after the fix. Canonical tests and targeted
source mutants cover the durable success watermark and admitted consumer seam.
---
